---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="Enterprise PAM Engineering"
  description="Enterprise Privileged Access Management (PAM) case study: credential lifecycle automation, session governance, and integration architecture across AD/Entra ID and cloud IAM."
  ogType="article"
>
  <section class="px-6 pb-20 pt-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div data-reveal>
        <a href="/work/" class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-textMuted transition-colors duration-300 hover:text-accent">
          <svg class="h-4 w-4" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m12 19-7-7 7-7"/><path d="M19 12H5"/></svg>
          Back to Work
        </a>
        <span class="block text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-textMuted">Case Study</span>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-balance text-4xl font-bold leading-tight text-textMain md:text-6xl">Enterprise PAM Engineering</h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-pretty text-lg leading-relaxed text-textMuted">
          Senior Solutions Architect and PAM subject matter expert at Netwrix, designing and deploying enterprise privileged access and identity management solutions for complex environments.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 pb-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="100">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-bold text-textMain">Scope</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-4">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
            <span class="leading-relaxed text-textMuted">Credential lifecycle automation using Python, PowerShell, and API-driven orchestration.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
            <span class="leading-relaxed text-textMuted">Session governance through proxied recording, monitoring, and just-in-time access controls.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
            <span class="leading-relaxed text-textMuted">Service account policy enforcement with vaulting, rotation, and risk-based access pathways.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 pb-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="200">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-bold text-textMain">Integration Architecture</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-textMuted">
          <p class="text-pretty">
            Designed PAM integration patterns tying together SIEM/SOAR telemetry, ITSM workflows, and CI/CD deployment controls. The objective was not just control enforcement, but resilient, auditable operations with minimal friction for delivery teams.
          </p>
          <p class="text-pretty">
            Implementations emphasized deterministic onboarding, clean rollback paths, and measurable policy compliance.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 pb-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="300">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-bold text-textMain">Result</h2>
        <p class="text-pretty leading-relaxed text-textMuted">
          Delivered enterprise-grade privileged access platforms with repeatable automation patterns and governance models that held up under audit and production pressure.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 rounded-xl border border-accent/20 bg-accent/5 p-6">
          <p class="text-sm font-mono text-accent">Netwrix Hero Award &mdash; Q1 FY&apos;25</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-textMuted">Excellence in enterprise PAM solution delivery</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
